Chapter: FwdGeneticAlgorithmTest
  cites AI chapter GeneticAlgorithm

 This test used to print "AI/GeneticAlgorithm OK" and call nothing. It proved
 the chapter compiled and could not fail for any other reason, which is the
 shape the lesson index calls L-FALSIF. The same defect in
 the app copy of this algorithm was real: sort-by-fitness there was once a
 stub that returned the population unchanged, and the GA still ran, still
 bred, still mutated, and never selected on fitness at all.

 So the first thing asserted here is that the ranking actually reorders. A
 selection step that does nothing is invisible from outside, because a GA
 without selection produces output shaped exactly like a GA with it.

Section: Fixtures

  mk-chromo : Integer -> GaChromosome
  mk-chromo (v) = GaChromosome { genes = [v, v + 1, v + 2], gene-count = 3 }

  head-gene : GaChromosome -> Integer
  head-gene (c) = list-at (c.genes) 0

  head-genes : List GaChromosome, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  head-genes (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let sep = if i == 0 then "" else " "
    in head-genes xs (i + 1) n (acc & sep & show (head-gene (list-at xs i)))

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let pop = [mk-chromo 11, mk-chromo 22, mk-chromo 33, mk-chromo 44]
    in let scores = [1, 9, 3, 7]
    in let ranked = ga-rank pop scores
    in let kept = ga-take ranked 2
    in let stepped = ga-elitist-step pop scores 2 ga-chromo-breed ga-chromo-mutate 5
    in let gp = GaPopulation { individuals = pop, fitness = scores, pop-size = 4, gene-count = 3, generation = 0 }
    in let evolved = ga-evolve-elitist gp 2 5
    in act
      print-line-uni ("ranked:   " & head-genes ranked 0 (list-length ranked) "")
      print-line-uni ("kept:     " & head-genes kept 0 (list-length kept) "")
      print-line-uni ("stepped:  " & show (list-length stepped) & " individuals")
      print-line-uni ("elite held: " & head-genes stepped 0 2 "")
      print-line-uni ("best-idx: " & show (ga-best-idx gp))
      print-line-uni ("best-fit: " & show (ga-best-fitness gp))
      print-line-uni ("avg-fit:  " & show (ga-avg-fitness gp))
      print-line-uni ("evolved gen: " & show (evolved.generation))
      print-line-uni ("evolved size: " & show (list-length (evolved.individuals)))
    end
